We build a finite-horizon two-player game~\parencite{OsborneRubinstein1994} played \emph{backward} from the output, with unit mass at the positive output state. A state records layer, neuron, player turn and stream sign;
stopping moves to an absorbing cemetery state $\dagger$. Skip connections become random transitions to
summand states; max-pooling sends players greedily to maximal-payoff states.
